<!-- 3 SERVICES -->
<section class="light" id="services"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">What we build and run</p>
 <h2>Seven roofing marketing services, one connected system</h2>
 <p class="lead">A marketing system with seven parts performs at the level of its weakest one. The <a href="/6-gap-revenue-map/">6-Gap Revenue Map™</a> shows which part is leaking most, and we start there, often on the calls you already get.</p>
 <div class="tlax" aria-hidden="true"><span>Marketing that brings the call</span><span>Sales systems that sign the roof</span></div>
 <ol class="tline">
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="svp1"><span class="tn">01</span><span class="tw">Generate targeted demand</span><span class="th">Google Ads and Local Services Ads</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp1" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb1"><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">01 · Generate targeted demand</p><p>Google Ads and Local Services Ads for roofing companies, built by service and city, filtered against DIY and "how to patch a roof" searches, and judged on cost per signed job. Emergency repair, full replacement and storm damage each get their own campaigns. Meta ads and retargeting stay in front of homeowners comparing quotes, and direct mail reaches neighborhoods after a storm. <a class="tl" href="/services/ppc-for-contractors/">PPC for contractors <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 2–4 weeks, in new inspection requests.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp2"><span class="tn">02</span><span class="tw">Build lasting local visibility</span><span class="th">Local SEO and Google Maps</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp2" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb2" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">02 · Build lasting local visibility</p><p>Local SEO for roofing companies: a fully built Google Business Profile that wins the map pack in the towns you roof, then the pages behind it for every service and city you serve: "roof replacement [city]," "roof repair near me," "storm damage roof repair," "metal roof installation." <a class="tl" href="/local-contractor-seo-blueprint/">Local SEO for contractors <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 3–6 months, then compounds for years.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp3"><span class="tn">03</span><span class="tw">Own your lead source</span><span class="th">Exclusive leads you own</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp3" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb3" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">03 · Own your lead source</p><p>Exclusive roofing leads, generated, not bought: homeowners who called you and only you, from a marketing engine you keep. No HomeAdvisor, no Angi bidding wars, no three other roofers calling the same house. <a class="tl" href="/lead-generation-for-service-businesses/">Lead generation <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> as the mix shifts, with close rates in a different class.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp4"><span class="tn">04</span><span class="tw">Turn searches into inspections</span><span class="th">A website that books the inspection</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp4" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb4" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">04 · Turn searches into inspections</p><p>A fast roofing website that turns searches into inspection requests: pages for each service and city, your finished roofs and reviews where the decision happens, financing and the insurance claim process explained in plain words, and one next step.</p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 4–8 weeks, across every channel.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp5"><span class="tn">05</span><span class="tw">Win the comparison</span><span class="th">Reviews and referrals</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp5" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb5" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">05 · Win the comparison</p><p>Reviews and referrals that compound: every customer asked for a review after every roof, every review answered, negative reviews handled, and referrals asked for while the new roof is still the talk of the street. Homeowners spending five figures read reviews before they call. <a class="tl" href="/services/reputation-management-for-contractors/">Reputation <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 2–3 months, then every month after.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp6"><span class="tn">06</span><span class="tw">Convert the calls you get</span><span class="th">Speed to lead and estimate follow-up</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp6" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb6" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">06 · Convert the calls you get</p><p>First contact in minutes, the inspection booked and confirmed, the no-show prevented, then every estimate followed up until it's signed or lost, including the homeowner waiting on financing or an insurance adjuster. The marketing you already paid for, finally answered. It lifts every channel above at once. <a class="tl" href="/services/lead-to-booked-job/">How it works <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> this week, on calls you already get.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp7"><span class="tn">07</span><span class="tw">Connect marketing to signed jobs</span><span class="th">Attribution to the signed job</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp7" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb7" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">07 · Connect marketing to signed jobs</p><p>Every call, form and inspection tagged to its source and followed to sold or lost, so each channel's true cost per signed job decides next month's budget. You always know the lead source, the cost per lead, the close rate and the return. <a class="tl" href="/attribution/">How we measure it <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> every month.</p></div></li>
 </ol>
 <p class="tlhint">Tap any step for what it covers.</p>
</div></section>

<!-- 4 MATH: table + calculator -->
<section class="soft" id="math"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">What the marketing gap costs</p>
 <h2>In roofing marketing, the next roof is often already <span class="o">on your estimate list.</span></h2>
 <p class="lead">Your marketing report ends at the lead. Your business runs on the signed job, and the two can point in opposite directions.</p>
 <table class="cmp rpt">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">The report says</th><th scope="col">The decision it drives</th><th scope="col">What's really happening</th><th scope="col">What we'd do</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
   <tr><th scope="row">"Storm calls are pouring in."</th><td data-l="The decision it drives">Push more ads into the hit zip codes.</td><td data-l="What's really happening">The office can't book inspections fast enough. Homeowners sign with the first roofer on the roof.</td><td data-l="What we'd do">Fix call response and inspection booking first, then decide whether more spend is needed.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">"Leads are up again."</th><td data-l="The decision it drives">Buy more marketing.</td><td data-l="What's really happening">Inspections get run and estimates go out, but too few turn into signed jobs.</td><td data-l="What we'd do">Review close rates, estimate follow-up, financing and the insurance handoff, and work the open estimates you already paid for.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">"Let's push harder before winter."</th><td data-l="The decision it drives">Spend more to fill the schedule.</td><td data-l="What's really happening">Crews are already booked for weeks, and weather limits install days.</td><td data-l="What we'd do">Weigh crew capacity and margins. Aim demand at the most profitable roofs or add crews before scaling.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
 <div class="calc" id="calc">
  <h3>What's one more roof in ten estimates worth to you?</h3>
  <p class="sub">Same estimates, same marketing budget, a higher close rate. Change the numbers to yours. Nothing you enter is&nbsp;saved.</p>
  <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Close rate lift"><button type="button" data-v="5" aria-pressed="false">+5 points of close rate</button><button type="button" data-v="10" aria-pressed="true">+10 points · one more roof in ten</button></div>
  <div class="cgrid">
   <div class="ins">
    <div><label for="rfEst">Roof estimates per month</label><output id="rfEstOut">20</output><input type="range" id="rfEst" min="4" max="150" step="1" value="20"></div>
    <div><label for="rfJob">Average roof job</label><output id="rfJobOut">$9,611</output><input type="range" id="rfJob" min="3000" max="60000" step="1" value="9611"></div>
    <div><label for="rfCr">Your close rate today</label><output id="rfCrOut">30%</output><input type="range" id="rfCr" min="5" max="70" step="1" value="30"></div>
   </div>
   <div class="res" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="k">Added roofing revenue a year, from the same estimates</p>
    <p class="big"><span id="rfAdd">+$230,664</span> <small id="rfMore">2 more signed jobs a month.</small></p>
    <p class="gp" id="rfRate">30% → 40% close rate.</p>
    <p class="now" id="rfCap">Can your crews install 2 more roofs a month? If not, that's the first limit to fix, before any new marketing.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <details class="how"><summary>Sources and how it's calculated</summary><p>Added revenue = estimates per month × 12 × average roof × close-rate lift: 20 × 12 × $9,611 × 10% = $230,664. Average roof replacement $9,611, with most homeowners paying $5,903–$13,380 (Angi, updated Oct 2026, 32,999 projects). Twenty estimates a month and a 30% close rate are starting points, not benchmarks. This is revenue, not profit. Illustration, not a client result.</p></details>
 </div>
 <p class="midcta"><a class="btn" href="https://calendly.com/andrew-andrewryanmarketing/gap-review?utm_source=arm-site&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=site&amp;utm_content=rf-mid">Let's talk about your marketing&nbsp;<span class="ar">→</span></a><span>Bring your real numbers. We'll run them with you.</span></p>
</div></section>

<!-- 5 WHERE JOBS ARE WON OR LOST + GROWTH PATHS -->
<section class="light" id="leaks"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">Where the roof is won or lost</p>
 <h2>Most agencies report the first step. The roof is decided in the last three.</h2>
 <p class="lead">A homeowner buys a roof rarely, often under pressure from a leak or a storm, calls several roofers, and decides after the inspection. A marketing report that ends at the phone call sees none of that. We follow it to the signed job.</p>
 <ol class="path">
  <li><span class="st">1 · The search</span><b>Found isn't chosen</b><h3>"Roof replacement near me"</h3><p>Your ad, map listing or page has to win the click, then the call or the form.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">2 · The call</span><b>Reached in 5 minutes</b><h3>Before another roofer calls back</h3><p>After a storm, the homeowner calls three companies. The first one to answer usually gets on the roof.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">3 · The inspection</span><b>Inspected isn't signed</b><h3>Inspected, priced, financed</h3><p>The inspection, the estimate, the financing or insurance question, and the follow-up decide it. Most agencies never see this step.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">4 · The install</span><b>The only number that pays&nbsp;you</b><h3>Signed and installed</h3><p>Crews and weather decide how much demand you can use, so marketing never outruns what your crews can install.</p></li>
 </ol>
 <h3 class="h3x">Where should your next million in roofs come from?</h3>
 <div class="paths3">
  <div><p class="tag">Own your home market</p><h4>You're known in town. The storm chasers still get the first call.</h4><p>Take the map pack, the reviews and the inspection path in the towns you already roof.</p><a class="tl" href="/local-contractor-seo-blueprint/">See what it takes <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
  <div><p class="tag">Open the next market</p><h4>New town, no reviews, no referrals.</h4><p>See the cost per signed job there before you hire a crew or open a second location.</p><a class="tl" href="/contractor-growth-marketing/">Model the next market <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
  <div><p class="tag">Close more of what you run</p><h4>The inspections get run, but too few sign.</h4><p>Fix the callback, the set and the close before you buy more demand.</p><a class="tl" href="/services/lead-to-booked-job/">Fix the second funnel <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
 </div>
</div></section>

