<!-- 7 ENGAGEMENT -->
<section class="light" id="engagement"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">How we work with roofing companies</p>
 <h2>Three ways to buy roofing marketing. Only one leaves you owning the engine.</h2>
 <table class="cmp">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">What you're comparing</th><th scope="col">Lead marketplaces</th><th scope="col">A generalist marketing agency</th><th scope="col">Andrew Ryan Marketing</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
   <tr><th scope="row">Who else gets the lead</th><td data-l="Lead marketplaces">Three or four other roofers, at once.</td><td data-l="A generalist marketing agency">Often another client of theirs in your market.</td><td data-l="Andrew Ryan Marketing">Nobody. One roofing company per market, in writing.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">What gets measured</th><td data-l="Lead marketplaces">Leads delivered.</td><td data-l="A generalist marketing agency">Traffic, rankings, calls, and a monthly PDF.</td><td data-l="Andrew Ryan Marketing">Cost per signed job by channel, every month.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">When you spend more</th><td data-l="Lead marketplaces">Whenever you want more volume.</td><td data-l="A generalist marketing agency">When the agency recommends it.</td><td data-l="Andrew Ryan Marketing">When the numbers prove it, and after we check the crews can install it.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">What you keep</th><td data-l="Lead marketplaces">Nothing. Stop paying, the marketing stops.</td><td data-l="A generalist marketing agency">Often not the ad accounts, tracking or data.</td><td data-l="Andrew Ryan Marketing">Your site, ad accounts, data and reporting, from day one.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
 <div class="notyet">
  <div>
   <h3>Sometimes the answer on more marketing is: not yet.</h3>
   <p>Anyone quoting "5–10% of revenue" before asking your close rate is guessing with your money. The real question is what it costs to sign one roof today, and whether the next dollar returns more than it costs. Sometimes the crews, not the demand, are the limit. We will say so, and show you the math.</p>
   <p><b>Build before the storm, harvest after it.</b> Storms don't wait for your rankings. SEO takes months to compound and paid campaigns need weeks of data, so the roofer already ranking and reviewed catches storm demand without chasing it. <a class="tl" href="/pricing/">See every price range <span class="ar">→</span></a></p>
  </div>
